ficant figures from world wars the  end of the war pretty much marks the end  of the video but scotzini is a bit  different because in many ways his crazy  story is only just getting started  like many of his fellow nazis he was  tried at dachau on charges of war crimes  specifically for impersonating enemy  soldiers during the battle of the bulge  an act that contravenes the  international rules of war scotsini was  eventually acquitted of any wrongdoing  and oddly enough the key evidence that  got him off was provided in testimony  from famous british secret agent wing  commander forrest frederick edward yo  thomas better known as the white rabbit  yo thomas testified that allied special  forces had themselves used nazi uniforms  as disguises in similar covert  operations and since there was no  evidence scorcini and his men had worn  the american uniforms during battle  which was actually the illegal bit he  was ultimately set free  incidentally there's another 007  connection here joe thomas is considered  by many to have been ian fleming's main  inspiration for the character of james  bond scotzini wasn't after hook yet  though several european countries filed  their own grievances against him for his  actions during the war and he remained  in custody until those offences could be  heard in court but of course that day  never came because scotcini had no  intention of spending the rest of his  life rotting away in jail and in the  summer of 1948 he escaped from his cell  or more accurately he was busted out in  a strange parallel of his actions during  the battle of the bulge  three unidentified men turned up at the  camp where scotzini was being held  claiming they were under orders to take  him to a legal hearing the men appeared  to be american soldiers and so  scotzini's captors handed him over  without question little did they know  they'd just given europe's most  dangerous man to three of his former ss  comrades dressed in commandeered u.s  army uniforms  intriguingly scotzini later claimed that  the americans had actually been in on  his escape plot all along and had  willingly supplied his ss buddies with  official u.s uniforms to help the whole  thing go off without a hitch  it sounds ridiculous i know but  scotzini's whole life was fairly  ridiculous and it isn't beyond the  realms of possibility that there's at  least a kernel of truth in this one for  starters we do know that scott ceni was  in contact with american intelligence  agencies after the war after escaping  from prison he worked with another  ex-nazi called reinhard gellen who spent  his post-war years in charge of the  cia-affiliated  gallon organization it's also  interesting that whilst he did move  around a fair bit after escaping prison  including spending some time in germany  france austria and eventually settling  in general franco's spain scotzini  wasn't exactly hounded to the end of the  earth like the fugitive he was supposed  to be in fact within a few years his  life went pretty much back to normal  he was even declared officially  de-nazified in 1952 by a west german  de-nazification cause  despite never actually appearing in  front of them that essentially allowed  him to do as he pleased and so he opened  up an import export business in madrid a  business that made scotzini a wealthy  man  whilst most of his dealings seem to have  been legitimate there was one particular  export product that most certainly did  not appear on the balance sheet  nazis you've probably heard that a lot  of nazis escaped justice in europe by  fleeing to south america after the war  and it seems that scotzini played an  important role in helping many of them  to get there rumor has it he used his  spanish company as a front for an  organization called d spinner that's  german for the spider which is thought  to have helped as many as 600 ex-nazis  flee to south america where they dreamt  of initiating the so-called for frank  whilst official details are fairly fit  on the ground when it comes to d spinner  there's plenty of evidence that scotzini  spent a significant amount of time in  argentina during the period long enough  to meet with the president juan peron  and briefly to become the bodyguard of  his wife eva better known as avita  according to scotzini's own account he  once saved avita's life during an  attempted assassination  for which of course she was very  grateful  so grateful according to some that the  two went on to have a passionate affair  i told you he was hitler's answer to  james bond  speaking of bond there's yet another  connection here ian fleming is said to  have baited blofeld's specter  organization on d spinner in part as a  kind of warning as to what might happen  if nazis like scotzini were allowed to  walk free  during the 1950s scotzini was offered a  job by muhammad nagoob who just seized  power in egypt during the egyptian  revolution perhaps keen to get out of  europe considering the whole holocaust  thing he'd just been helping out with  scotzini accepted going on to act as a  military advisor while helping to train  the egyptian army in guerilla warfare  and commando tactics including  incidentally a young recruit by the name  eviassa arafat  scotzini's story is a roller coaster by  all accounts but his final assignment  provides quite possibly the most  disorientating loop the loop of the  whole runaway tale because in a plot  twist not even m night shyamalan could  have seen coming in 1963 scotzini was  secretly recruited by mossad now in case  you aren't familiar with the  organization mossad is the name of the  israeli secret service or to put that  another way scotzini a prominent nazi  who played an active role in the  holocaust went and got himself a job  with the secret service of the country  of the largest jewish population on  earth not exactly an ideal foundation  for a business partnership i'm sure  you'll agree to make things even more  confusing mossad essentially recruited  scotzini who was still very much an  active nazi no matter what the  de-nazification courts might have  decided to become a nazi hunter on the  face of it it was a genuinely baffling  turn of events  but there were deeper motivations at  play here rumor has it mossad had  initially considered having scotzini  murdered  for obvious reasons but that they  eventually came to the conclusion he was  more valuable working with them than  buried somewhere in an unmarked grave  you see back in the 60s egypt recruited  a large number of german scientists  who'd previously developed the world's  first long-range guided ballistic  missile the v2 rocket for hitler during  the second world war understanding that  it was only a matter of time before  these rockets will be pointed towards  israel  mossad initiated operation damocles to  disrupt their development as much as  possible and that's where scotzini came  in as a senior member of the nazi party  who had strong ties to the egyptian  military  he was not only able to provide plenty  of information on egypt's rocket  programme he also personally knew many  of the scientists who'd been recruited  to staff it  as for why scotzini agreed to betray his  former colleagues to help out israel  well it turns out that not everyone had  forgiven him for his actions during the  war and one of those people was jewish  austrian holocaust survivor turned  famous nazi hunter simon weisenfall it  was common knowledge that weizenfall had  a list of ex-nazis he plans to bring to  justice and scotsie and he happened to  know that his name was on it and so he  agreed to work with mossad on one  condition  that they make his name disappear from  weisenfall's list  during his time working for the israelis  it's alleged that scotzini was a key  part of a terror campaign against a nazi  scientist working on egypt's rocket  programme which included abductions  threats against the scientists families  and the posting of letter bombs that led  to at least five deaths it's also  alleged that scotcini carried out a hit  on senior scientist heinz krug executing  him in the woods outside of munich  before having his body dissolved in acid  to hide the evidence  despite the work he did for mossad  scotzini never quite denounced his nazi  past quite the opposite in fact along  with d spinner he set up at least two  other neo-nazi organizations the paladin  group and sidade  and remained true to his ideology of his  beloved fuhrer until his death from lung  cancer in madrid in 1975.  the funeral was attended by many of  scotsini's former ss comrades who showed  their true colours by giving the nazi  salute and singing several of hitler's  favorite songs yeah so much for  denazification hey  it's hard to miss the brutal injustice  in this story despite the many terrible  things scott cena did in his life not to  mention the countless terrible things he  supported others doing he died a wealthy  man in possession of luxurious  properties across europe he married  twice drove expensive cars and rubbed  shoulders with some of the most  important people in the world in the end  otto scorsini is a shining example of an  uncomfortable and yet undeniable truth  that's no matter how terrible a person  you may be if you have friends in high  places who consider you to be valuable  you can quite literally get away with  murder  thanks for watching
 

